Tells the core (//browser_core/drm_request.mojom) which protected-media key system a page asks
for, so the app can say why a site's video won't play. requestMediaKeySystemAccess is answered
in the renderer, and the browser never hears of it: the Blink encrypted media module's
initializer base, which both it and MediaCapabilities make, calls the core's per-frame
interface, and the core adds its binder to a frame's through g_browser_core_populate_frame_binders
(//browser_core/hooks.h). What a request means is the core's to decide; nothing comes back.

